2:T8ae,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How many form fields is too many for a cold-traffic landing page?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Five or fewer for cold traffic. Name, email, and the minimum context needed to deliver what you promised. Company size, phone number, and budget questions belong on a qualification call, not the entry form. Every additional field you add to cold-traffic forms costs completions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should the form submit button say?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It should state what the visitor receives, not what they're doing. 'Submit' and 'Send' describe the visitor's action. 'Get my free audit', 'Book the call', 'Start my trial' describe the outcome. The outcome framing converts better because it reminds the visitor why they're filling out the form."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does removing the phone number field actually increase form completions?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, consistently. Phone number is the single highest-friction field on lead gen forms for cold traffic. Unless phone is required for your delivery workflow, remove it from the entry form and collect it on a follow-up step after the initial conversion."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where should social proof be placed on a lead gen landing page?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Adjacent to the form, not below it. A testimonial or client logo strip positioned directly above or beside the submit button acts at the moment of commitment - when trust is most needed. Proof at the bottom of the page, after the CTA, is too late for the visitors who abandoned without scrolling."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is 'post-submit clarity' and why does it matter?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It's the statement of what happens after the visitor clicks submit. 'We'll be in touch' creates anxiety - when? From whom? For what? 'You'll receive your report in 2 minutes by email' eliminates the uncertainty. Visitors who know exactly what to expect immediately after submitting are less likely to abandon the thank-you page or mark the follow-up as spam."}}]}6:X
