f:["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6 mb-3 pl-7","children":"'Submit' and 'Send' are system verbs - they describe what the visitor is doing, not what they receive. On a cold-traffic form, the button label is the final moment of decision. A label that reminds the visitor of the outcome ('Get my free audit', 'Book the call', 'Send my report') reaffirms the exchange value at exactly the moment the visitor needs it most."}]
10:["$","div",null,{"className":"pl-7 border-l-2 border-accent/30 ml-7","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wider mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Replace the generic verb with the outcome statement. Match it to the ad promise. If the ad said 'free audit in 2 minutes', the button should say 'Get my free audit'. The label should be specific enough that a visitor who skimmed the page could infer what they signed up for from the button alone."}]]}]
11:["$","div","2",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 mb-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mt-0.5","children":"03"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-0.5","children":"Social proof"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold text-fg","children":"No proof adjacent to the form"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6 mb-3 pl-7","children":"The moment of highest friction on a lead gen page is the instant before the visitor clicks submit. That is when trust is most needed and most absent. Most pages place testimonials and client logos in a section below the form - where only visitors who scroll past the CTA will see them. Cold traffic that bounces without scrolling never receives the trust signal."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"pl-7 border-l-2 border-accent/30 ml-7","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wider mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Position one testimonial or logo strip directly above or beside the submit button - inside the form container or immediately adjacent to it. A single named quote with a specific outcome outperforms a logo strip. Job title and company are sufficient attribution."}]]}]]}]
12:["$","div","3",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 mb-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mt-0.5","children":"04"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-0.5","children":"Above the fold"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold text-fg","children":"The form is below the fold on mobile"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6 mb-3 pl-7","children":"On mobile, many lead gen pages place the form below a hero section, an explanation of the offer, and a bullet-point feature list. The visitor arrives from an ad on a 375px screen and sees a headline and hero image - no form, no CTA. Visitors who don't scroll don't convert. The form being below the fold on mobile is the most structurally invisible failure on lead gen pages."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"pl-7 border-l-2 border-accent/30 ml-7","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wider mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"On mobile, place the form - or at minimum the email field and submit button - within the first viewport. The headline states the offer; the form captures it. Supporting content goes below. If the layout cannot support a form above the fold, use a single-field email capture with full form on the next step."}]]}]]}]
13:["$","div","4",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 mb-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mt-0.5","children":"05"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-0.5","children":"Privacy micro-copy"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold text-fg","children":"No 'no spam' assurance adjacent to the email field"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6 mb-3 pl-7","children":"Cold traffic is skeptical about email capture. The visitor's implicit concern - 'will this result in daily marketing emails?' - goes unaddressed on most lead gen forms. A single line adjacent to the email field ('No spam. Unsubscribe any time.') directly answers the objection at the moment it arises. Its absence is not neutral - it leaves the concern unanswered."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"pl-7 border-l-2 border-accent/30 ml-7","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wider mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Add a single line of micro-copy directly below the email input. Keep it specific: 'No spam. Unsubscribe any time.' or 'One email with your report. Nothing else.' Do not use generic privacy policy links as a substitute - the visitor is looking for a human assurance, not a legal document."}]]}]]}]
14:["$","div","5",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 mb-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mt-0.5","children":"06"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-0.5","children":"Post-submit clarity"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold text-fg","children":"No statement of what happens after submission"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6 mb-3 pl-7","children":"'We'll be in touch' creates three unanswered questions: when, from whom, and for what purpose. A visitor who submits a form and receives ambiguous confirmation has no framework for what to do next. They cannot confirm the submission worked. They cannot anticipate the follow-up. Uncertainty after submission increases abandon rate on the thank-you page and increases spam reports on the follow-up email."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"pl-7 border-l-2 border-accent/30 ml-7","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wider mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Replace the confirmation message with a specific delivery statement: 'You'll receive your audit by email in 2 minutes. Check your inbox - and spam folder if needed.' State the delivery channel, the delivery time, and the content. This is the contract the visitor agreed to - confirm it explicitly."}]]}]]}]
15:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-14","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg mb-4","children":"What the audit checks on a lead gen page"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6 mb-6 max-w-2xl","children":"Nebula checks the same 9 signals on every URL. For lead gen pages, the signals that fail most often are form field count, CTA label, and proof proximity. The audit returns pass/fail with the raw value from your page - field count, button label, trust markers in source order - so every finding is verifiable."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","div","Form field count",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-2","children":"Form field count"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-fg-muted leading-5 mb-1","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent","children":"Pass: "}],"5 fields or fewer for cold traffic"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-fg-muted leading-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-signal-fail","children":"Fail: "}],"6+ required fields on the entry form"]}]]}],["$","div","CTA label",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-2","children":"CTA label"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-fg-muted leading-5 mb-1","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent","children":"Pass: "}],"Button states what the visitor receives"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-fg-muted leading-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-signal-fail","children":"Fail: "}],"Button says 'Submit' or 'Send'"]}]]}],["$","div","Social proof",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-